  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    K-Beauty, Explained is a blog written for readers outside Korea who are
    curious about Korean skincare and beauty — routines, ingredients, and
    products, and why they work the way they do. Posts start as AI-assisted
    drafts and are reviewed and edited by a human before publishing, with the
    goal of adding original, practical detail rather than just summarizing
    what's already online.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is written and edited by Chris Kim, who reviews, fact-checks, and
    edits every post before it's published.
  </p>
  <p>
    Have a topic suggestion or a correction? Reach out via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
